WHDLoad.Audio - CD-DA plugin for WHDLoad
----------------------------------------

CDTV and CD32 games play their music as CD-DA tracks from the CD. Under
WHDLoad these tracks are replaced by compressed audio files, which are played
via additional audio hardware.
The plugin WHDLoad.Audio contains the hardware drivers. WHDLoad loads the
tracks and calls the plugin via resload_Audio (requires WHDLoad 21+).

Usage:
- copy WHDLoad.Audio to the directory where WHDLoad is located
- set the option Audio/K (Tooltype or CLI) to the directory with the tracks
- the tracks are named trackNN.<ext>, NN = CD track number 01..99
  (e.g. track02.mp3), case does not matter
- the game must use level 2 interrupts (PORTS) and WHDLoad must be able to
  move the VBR, otherwise there is no music

Build:
	make		build WHDLoad.Audio (vasm or basm)
	make clean	remove all generated artefacts

The plugin consists of a single hunk. On init all drivers are probed until the
first one finds its hardware.

AmiGUS driver (amigus.s)
------------------------

https://github.com/necronomfive/AmiGUS-pub

- supported cards: AmiGUS (Zorro II) and AmiGUS mini (PCMCIA, interrupt via
  Gayle)
- requires amigus.library, the codec part of the card is reserved while
  WHDLoad is running, if it is in use by another program audio is disabled
- decoding is done in hardware by the VS1063a codec, supported formats:
  mp3	MPEG 1/2 Layer III
  ogg	Ogg Vorbis
  flac	FLAC
  wav	WAV (PCM, IMA ADPCM)
  aac	AAC-LC, HE-AAC v2 (ADTS recommended, ADIF also possible)
  m4a	MPEG4 audio (AAC), the mdat atom must be the last atom in the file,
	convert if necessary (e.g. mp4creator -optimize)
  wma	WMA 2/7/8/9 (not WMA Pro/Voice)
  if multiple files exist for a track the first format in this list is used
- the codec fifo is fed from the level 2 interrupt (watermark 1024 words), no
  custom or cia registers are accessed
- looping restarts the stream directly from the start without stop, this
  works best with formats which resynchronize on frames (mp3, ogg, flac, aac
  ADTS), with the others (wav, m4a, wma) the file header is fed in the
  middle of the stream and may cause a click or glitch
- volume $0..$7fff is mapped to 128 steps of codec attenuation (0.5 dB steps,
  0 = silent)
- after the end of a track the end fill bytes are fed, so the codec finishes
  the decoding completely
- during OS switches of WHDLoad (e.g. loading files) the interrupt is disabled,
  the fifo plays out, longer OS actions may cause a gap in the music
- the VS1063a patches package 2.6 of VLSI Solution is loaded on init and
  after each codec reset (fixes e.g. FLAC and AAC decoding issues)
  https://www.vlsi.fi/en/support/software/vs10xxpatches.html
- the trace file (option Trace) shows card type, hardware and firmware
  revision and the result of the codec initialization
